    "intro": "Hi! Lesson 24 — **npm, Vite and modules**. Real projects have hundreds of files, and they must be assembled into a ready site. Let's go!",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "What npm is",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🛒",
            "text": "**npm** is a store of ready pieces of code, libraries. Why sew clothes from scratch if you can buy them?"
          },
          {
            "text": "Checking the install in the terminal:",
            "code": "node -v\nnpm -v"
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "npm",
            "prompt": "What is npm?",
            "options": [
              "A store of ready libraries",
              "A browser",
              "A programming language",
              "A game"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "npm is a package manager."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "A Vite project",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "⚡",
            "text": "We create a project:",
            "code": "npm create vite@latest"
          },
          {
            "text": "Folders and files appear: `src`, `index.html`, `package.json`. `package.json` is the **project passport**: which libraries are used and how to start the project."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "package.json",
            "prompt": "What is package.json?",
            "options": [
              "The project passport",
              "A picture",
              "A page style",
              "A browser"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "It lists libraries and run commands."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Installing and running",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "▶️",
            "text": "We install and run:",
            "code": "npm install     # install all libraries from package.json\nnpm run dev     # start a local server"
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "When you change code the page updates itself, no F5. It is called **hot reload**."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "Running",
            "prompt": "Which command starts the local server?",
            "options": [
              "npm run dev",
              "npm install",
              "npm create",
              "npm stop"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "npm run dev starts the dev server."
          },
          {
            "type": "input",
            "topic": "Running",
            "prompt": "What is the automatic page update on code change called? (two parts)",
            "answer": [
              "hot reload",
              "hotreload"
            ],
            "explain": "Hot reload — the page refreshes itself."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Modules: import and export",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🪟",
            "text": "The `utils.js` file puts a function on the «shop window»:",
            "code": "export function sum(a, b) {\n  return a + b;\n}"
          },
          {
            "text": "The `main.js` file takes it from the window:",
            "code": "import { sum } from \"./utils.js\";\nconsole.log(sum(2, 3)); // 5"
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "Practice: recreate the landing with Vite and split the JS into two files with `import` and `export`. Homework: push the project to GitHub as a new commit."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "match",
            "topic": "Modules",
            "prompt": "Match the word and meaning",
